Article 21

The regional government is obliged to assist in providing adequate special rooms for victims at the Resort Police Station (Pohes) and at every Sector Police station.

Article 22 (1) Social workers or volunteer personnel as referred to in Article 19 paragraph ' (1) letter b are tasked with accompanying victims in facing the process of resolving acts of violence.

2. Social workers or volunteer personnel in addition to being tasked as referred to in paragraph (1) carry out activities including:a. counseling or guidance to strengthen and provide a sense of security for victims;
b. providing information regarding the rights of victims to obtain protection from the police and the establishment of protection orders from the court;
c. escorting victims to safe houses or alternative residences; and d. carrying out integrated coordination in providing services to victims with agencies or related parties needed by victims.

Article 29

1. Forms of community participation may include: a. Supervision; or b. Provision of assistance;

(2) Community supervision includes activities:
a. observing or seeing the condition of the fulfillment of the rights of women and children; and b. providing information on any condition that tends to lead to acts of violence against women and children to the police apparatus and/or regional government.
3. Provision of assistance as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b shall be in the form of: a. securing or temporary shelter for victims;

b. financial support to meet the needs of victims according to the community's capacity;
c. Financial assistance and/or facilities to the regional government in supporting the implementation of protection for women and children.
